    "// A setext heading begins at the prose its underline folded up, not at the underline itself.",
    "/**\n * Where the deck divides: the separators the author wrote, plus the headings at the level in force.\n *\n * One set used to switch the other off, so a note with a rule in it lost its heading sections. The\n * two are read together now, and `buildDeck` drops the edges that land on an already-open slide.\n */",
    "/** Whether the lines between two cuts hold nothing to draw: blanks and a layout switch. A heading\n * under them has no slide of its own to open, because the cut above already starts the slide it would\n * begin — and a switch is a property of the slide rather than content on it, so paging it alone would\n * leave a slide that shows nothing and take the layout off the slide that asked for it. */",
    "// Cutting here too would make a page of the region's own blanks and hand the heading to it.",
    "// A separator only divides, so it belongs to no slide; a heading is the first line of",
    "// the slide it opens.",
    "// Where the deck starts counting this slide: a heading counts from its own line, since the",
    "// caret sitting on a title means that title, while a caret before a divider still reads as",
