    "/**\n * R2 storage for the music library.\n *\n * Uploads and downloads never name a path: every key is derived here from the account id, a track id\n * and the format, which is why an object can only land under the `music/` prefix this deployment\n * backs up. The ledger that pays for these bytes lives in `MusicStore`; a write that would cross the\n * account quota is refused under a lease so two concurrent finalizations cannot both see room.\n *\n * Deleting through `deleteMusicObjects` is strict: a failed R2 delete is queued on the music cleanup\n * table before the error is rethrown, so the maintenance sweep retries it and the caller is not told\n * a deletion happened when the bytes are still there.\n */",
